    "body": "Bumps [body-parser](https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser) and [express](https://github.com/expressjs/express). These dependencies needed to be updated together.\nUpdates `body-parser` from 1.20.3 to 1.20.9\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/releases\">body-parser's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.20.9</h2>\n<h2>Important: Security</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Security fix for <a href=\"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-111181\">CVE-2026-111181</a> (<a href=\"https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/security/advisories/GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828\">GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Release: 1.20.9 by <a href=\"https://github.com/UlisesGascon\"><code>@​UlisesGascon</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/expressjs/body-parser/pull/779\">expressjs/body-parser#779</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/compare/1.20.8...1.20.9\">https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/compare/1.20.8...1.20.9</a></p>\n<h2>1.20.8</h2>\n<h2>Important</h2>\n<p><strong>Same code base as <a href=\"https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/releases/tag/1.20.7\">1.20.7</a>. This was created to test the new release process.</strong></p>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>ci: backport npm-publish workflow from master by <a href=\"https://github.com/UlisesGascon\"><code>@​UlisesGascon</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/expressjs/body-parser/pull/769\">expressjs/body-parser#769</a></li>\n<li>1.20.8 by <a href=\"https://github.com/UlisesGascon\"><code>@​UlisesGascon</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/expressjs/body-parser/pull/770\">expressjs/body-parser#770</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/compare/1.20.7...1.20.8\">https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/compare/1.20.7...1.20.8</a></p>\n<h2>1.20.7</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>docs: include security fix in 1.20.6 changes by <a href=\"https://github.com/UlisesGascon\"><code>@​UlisesGascon</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/expressjs/body-parser/pull/747\">expressjs/body-parser#747</a></li>\n<li>deps: qs@~6.16.0 by <a href=\"https://github.com/krzysdz\"><code>@​krzysdz</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/expressjs/body-parser/pull/761\">expressjs/body-parser#761</a></li>\n<li>1.20.7 by <a href=\"https://github.com/UlisesGascon\"><code>@​UlisesGascon</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/expressjs/body-parser/pull/767\">expressjs/body-parser#767</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/compare/1.20.6...1.20.7\">https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/compare/1.20.6...1.20.7</a></p>\n<h2>1.20.6</h2>\n<h2>Important: Security</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Security fix for <a href=\"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2025-13466\">CVE-2026-12590</a> (<a href=\"https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/security/advisories/GHSA-v422-hmwv-36x6\">GHSA-v422-hmwv-36x6</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>fix: improve limit option validation by <a href=\"https://github.com/Phillip9587\"><code>@​Phillip9587</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/expressjs/body-parser/pull/741\">expressjs/body-parser#741</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/compare/1.20.5...1.20.6\">https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/compare/1.20.5...1.20.6</a></p>\n<h2>v1.20.5</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<p>The reason for this release is a fix to the extended urlencoded parser returning objects instead of arrays for large array inputs (&gt; 100) on exemplo@exemplo.invalid+. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/expressjs/body-parser/pull/716\">expressjs/body-parser#716</a>)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>refactor(json): simplify strict mode error string construction by <a href=\"https://github.com/jonchurch\"><code>@​jonchurch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://r…",
